        {
            "id": "ac1d8745-7f2c-4a54-9816-2fb433c475fc",
            "build_id": "a19913de-766a-40a0-8272-f95cfd525047",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-07-16T05:43:04.601249+00:00",
            "notes": "Our round 5 power is the first one where we have options based on who is on the enemy team. \n\nI typically go for Countermeasures, but if the enemy team has a Zarya or Orisa with the reflect power you should absolutely not take countermeasures as it will royally mess up your team. It's also not amazing into Sigma due to his shift ability. Additionally, if the enemy team has a DPS duo like Genji/Mei, you should not take Countermeasures because you just won't get much value from it. The ideal enemy comp for countermeasures is something like Rein/Soldier/Reaper/Zen/Kiriko as you will get tons of value and a bunch of free damage.\n\nVs the other heroes mentioned like Zarya, Orisa, and Mei, I like Party Protector. This scales with AP, and at this point we should have around 90% (with a fully charged Superflexor). This means our team gets almost double overheal from Party Protector, making it like a mini Lucio ult. You can get tons of value and save your team if you ult to counter a Zarya grav or Mei blizzard, or if Orisa/Sigma get a big ult on your team. \n\nFor items, its pretty similar to previous rounds. You should have Ordinance Onslaught and Cybervenom in almost all games by now. Your third purple can be Superflexor for raw AP (Superflexor plus Nano Cola is better than Champions Kit for raw AP), Liquid Nitrogen if you are against the aforementioned speedy characters like Queen or Soldier, OR you can go Catalytic Crystal if you want really fast ults to counter an enemy team comp that has something like Zarya and Mei together.",
