            "created_at": "2025-07-16T05:43:04.601249+00:00",
            "notes": "For our Round 7 power we have a couple options. I like Facetanking vs really bursty heroes like Cassidy, as eating a full fan the hammer will not only heal you a ton but also unleash about 1000 damage in rockets back at his face if you have Countermeasures. Facetanking will also not hurt your team vs a Zarya or reflecting Orisa, so you can take it even if you took Party Protector last round.\n\nIf you took Countermeasures, you can also take Facetanking, or you can go for Stat Boost for more matrix uptime. This power gets you more uptime than Ultrawide Matrix does, so I prefer it. \n\nFor items, just take as many purples as you can out of the ones we've mentioned. I'll list the top 4 purples that should be in every build in order of importance imo:\n\n1. Onslaught Ordinance\n2. Cybervenom\n3. Superflexor\n4. Champions Kit\n\nFor the final two, it depends on the enemy comp. Lumerico Fusion Drive is a good general item for damage and sustain with its Armor passive. As mentioned, Liquid Nitrogen is great into Soldier/Queen/Lucio. Catalytic Crystal is good if you have Party Protector and the enemy team has ults that are countered by a Lucio beat, so Zarya/Genji/Mei. Pulse Plating from the Survival Tree can also be a 6th purple to get ults even faster. This would synergize if you have Party Protector + Stat Boost for really fast mini Lucio beats for your team. Finally, Iridescent Iris is good for more raw AP+CDR .\n\nIf you don't have enough money for 6 purples just take Nano Cola or Multi Tool as your last item, whichever you have the money for.\n\nAs far as gameplay, its the same as all the previous rounds. Find isolated squishies and blow them up. Play from high ground and off angles and avoid engaging the enemy tank as much as possible until their entire team is dead behind them. You can basically blow up any squishy from max missile range at this point in the game, so you should run the lobby. The main struggles are teams with Zarya or Kiri, who can nullify your burst if they are good.",
